@@ -92,3 +92,29 @@ off-target outside the effect radius to guard against overly broad suppression.
 - Add a priest, paladin or other support bot to the duelist's group. During
   countdown and active duel it must not dispel, heal or buff either participant;
   the two participants' self-casts and hostile casts remain allowed.
+
+## Continuous spacing, forms, stealth and rogue setup
+
+- With a melee player continuously chasing a hunter, the hunter must issue one
+  long retreat path and keep running until at least 36 yards apart. Repeat for a
+  mage at 32 yards. Neither bot may stop at short intermediate endpoints; instant
+  slows and control remain usable while the movement spline stays active.
+- Keep a target inside the stable range band for ten seconds. The ranged bot must
+  hold position and hard cast. Move the target beyond the outer edge and verify
+  a continuous advance that stops at the preferred distance.
+- Blink while an old retreat path is active. The next retreat must replace the
+  old path immediately, without waiting for the old `LastMovement` delay.
+- Cast Divine Shield below 80% health while moving. The paladin must stop, heal,
+  and resume normal pressure once healthy instead of continuing its retreat.
+- Push a druid below 45% with an uncontrolled enemy in melee. It must remain in
+  Bear, use Bear survival/attacks, and leave form for healing only after control
+  lands or twelve yards of separation is established.
+- In a fresh rogue duel, verify `rogue-opener-sap`, rear reposition and either
+  Garrote against a caster/healer or Cheap Shot against melee. The rogue must
+  build five combo points before `rogue-five-point-kidney`, then activate Shadow
+  Dance and rebuild toward Eviscerate during the Kidney window.
+- Chase a resetting rogue. Its escape movement must remain continuous rather
+  than ending every few yards; Preparation is reserved for recovering Vanish.
+- Duel a stealthed rogue and repeat with multiple hostile bots nearby. A bot that
+  cannot personally detect the rogue must not target, move toward, range from, or
+  place an anti-stealth effect at the rogue's live hidden coordinates.
